TEXT 0 -416 Left 2 ;Problems 5 Q2a/b - condenser microphone with the Problem 1 values, T(s) = 1 (Gpb off: Tsw = 0)
TEXT 0 -384 Left 2 ;course circuit from the official solution: electrical and acoustical in the impedance analogy, electrostatic coupling as Norton current sources across Ce0 and Cmd
TEXT 0 -176 Left 2 ;ELECTRICAL: V(out) = output voltage [V] per 1 Pa
TEXT 1056 -176 Left 2 ;MECHANICAL (impedance analogy): I(Vd1) = diaphragm velocity u [m/s]
TEXT 0 304 Left 2 ;ACOUSTICAL (impedance analogy): V = pressure [Pa], I = volume velocity [m3/s].  back of the diaphragm (left) | front (right)
TEXT 0 1024 Left 2 !.param rho0=1.18 c0=344.0 rd=0.009 Epol=200 x0=2e-05 RL=5e+08 Vab=1e-06 Mmd=5e-05 Rmd=1 Cmd=4e-06 Mas=100 Ras=1e+07 Tsw=0
TEXT 0 1056 Left 2 !.param Sd=pi*rd**2 Ce0=8.85e-12*Sd/x0 Kel=Epol*Ce0/x0 Kmech=Epol*Cmd/x0 Cab2=Vab/(rho0*c0**2) Cab1=Cab2/200
TEXT 0 1088 Left 2 !.param Ma1=0.6133*rho0/(pi*rd) Ra1=0.5045*rho0*c0/(pi*rd**2) Ra2=rho0*c0/(pi*rd**2) Ca1=0.55*pi**2*rd**3/(rho0*c0**2) Kpb=Tsw/Ra2
TEXT 0 1200 Left 2 !.ac dec 1000 1 100k
TEXT 0 1232 Left 2 !.meas AC M250 FIND mag(V(out)) AT 250
TEXT 0 1296 Left 2 ;plot V(out): flat 9.82 mV/Pa (-40.2 dB re 1 V/Pa), peak at about 10 kHz (f0 = 10.62 kHz, Q = 2.36), then -12 dB/octave
TEXT 0 1328 Left 2 ;f0 = where the phase of V(out) has dropped 90 deg from its 250 Hz value;  Q = |V(out)| at f0 / |V(out)| at 250 Hz (linear)
TEXT 0 1360 Left 2 ;the official figure shows the Kel source as 1.1m: that is E*Ce0/x0 = 1.126m rounded, and it is why the official M250 reads 9.6 mV/Pa
